  "rationale": "Both answers fit the store-aisle sense, but the national split is materially overstated: lorong is shared, and kedai is an accepted Malay equivalent of toko while Indonesian usage also accepts kedai for shop/store. The relation should be revised from different-common-word to a regional-preference or shared-synonym relation. No false-friend contrast is needed.",
